  "summary": "Keys 1, 2 and 3 now select the glass, metal and fabric sphere. Only the selected sphere spins, at 0.6 rad/s about its vertical axis, and the other two keep their current angle. `window.__TASK_STATE__` has a new `selected` field typed `'glass' | 'metal' | 'fabric' | null`, which is `null` until a key is pressed. I changed `src/main.ts`, and typecheck passes. The final render still draws the same scene with no errors. I didn't press the keys in a browser, so the key handling and spin are untested.\n\nThe keydown handler matches on `e.code` (Digit1–3) and falls back to `e.key`. The three sphere nodes are now registered with `mutable: true` so their rotation can be set each frame. The glass sphere is uniform, so its spin shows only in the moving highlights and refraction."
